{"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","type":"reference"},{"text":" product to the test target. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"text":" binds a fresh","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker to the test’s task for the length of its body, then returns every event tracked in it, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. Here ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SignedUp"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func signingUpTracksThePlan() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker {","        Tracker.current.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","    }","    #expect(tracked.events(of: SignedUp.self) == [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")])","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call has a tracker of its own, so tests running at the same time never see each other’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events. The body may be sync or async, and may return a value, read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.value"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.names"},{"text":" lists every event’s name and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.records"},{"text":" every record.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most code needs nothing more: it tracks through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"type":"text","text":", which falls back to the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app bootstrapped, and the test’s binding wins over that one. A view whose tracker was never set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that binds its tracker with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" reaches the test’s tracker too. Pass a tracker instead where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"code reads one set for a single view tree. A tracker given to a SwiftUI view with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", such as a preview’s,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the view’s environment but not code that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"type":"text","text":". Such a test takes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker the body is given and sets it on the view: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"]}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"kind":"article","